The user outlined a detailed plan for a December Christmas photo note project involving early release, collaborative content updates, and a rescheduled event. They emphasized publishing the Christmas photo note on December 3 as a “prologue” that buyers can help update, postponing the main event from December 24 due to many followers having family commitments, and instead deciding the event date via a purchaser-limited poll for a day between December 20–25. The event (“Find Riko!”) involves a photo shoot with the first person to find Riko, with edited photos added back to the note by year-end.

I confirmed understanding and comprehensively reorganized the strategy and schedule to maximize natural engagement and sales flow for the Riko account. I provided a fully reconstructed December posting map including:

- Pre-release buildup posts (Dec 1–2);
- The December 3 prologue note launch with buyer participation and poll;
- Follow-up engagement and relevant “desire and warmth” themed posts through mid-December;
- Gift-style notes on Dec 10 and Dec 17 to deepen connection;
- Thank-you direct messages around Dec 18–19;
- The 20–25 event day with special posts and buyer interaction;
- Editing and processing photos Dec 26–30 with tasteful, meaningful posts;
- Final updated Christmas note release on Dec 31 linking into next year.

I also summarized quick answers for when asked what is already decided and invited the user to choose the next step—whether drafting posts from Nov 13 onward, the note text for Dec 3, or naming the event.
